This extension adds Deus Ex: Human Revolution modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]ModHook automatically installed.[/summary]

[b][color=#ffff00]The legacy and Director's Cut (DC) versions of the game are both supported, but most mods, including the ModHook, are only for the DC version.
[b][size=3]The extension will automatically download and install the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/deusexhumanrevolution/mods/28]DXHR Patcher with ModHook[/url][url=https://github.com/gibbed/DXHRDC-ModHook] [/url](Director's Cut only).[/size][/b][/color][/b]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]GOG[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Mods with a ".000" file install to the "mods" folder.[/*]
[*]DXHR Patcher installs to the game folder, recognised by a "DXHR-Patcher_1.5.jar" file.[/*]
[*]DXHRDC-ModHook mods with a "DFEngine.dll" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Automatically downloads and install the [url=https://github.com/gibbed/DXHRDC-ModHook]ModHook [/url]﻿to the game root folder.[/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Deus Ex: Human Revolution mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Mod .000 File:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".000" file.

  Installs to: "mods"

========================================================================

DXHR Patcher:

Recognised when the archive contains a "DXHR-Patcher_1.5.jar" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

DXHRDC-ModHook:

Recognised when the archive contains a "DFEngine.dll" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]

